cademy-id "q-17357" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+{50}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=-{1}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘},\\,x={b}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+{50}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 5x+{50}^{∘} & ={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =-{5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={265}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & =-{1}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={53}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=53.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-17357/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17357"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42790/selection/095bebe4de0692acffa7bacc05ea08bcb909f8b4ab3f78ce7297f4b408c7599e" :answer/id #uuid "86654b7b-321e-5fc5-8363-d6be7b49633a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42790/selection/f877c20246cdffb02c0bf1049751cbded026a1167735517391df4b4eb845057e" :answer/id #uuid "f55b8f6b-06b7-50bf-a065-0ff2ceca6393" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42790/selection/f3fdc5822158ade5c249480916c64d7cab4e389e7f8ac32e87429a4d3ff044da" :answer/id #uuid "d77e274e-acdc-5e25-9edc-a553bb6e1f36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42790/selection/19dc865f9e5e3c737c66357f8fadabd198054c3b810769ac94279915b38d6a76" :answer/id #uuid "f7aa660e-6667-5069-